{"id": "family-shelter-beds-left-empty", "title": "Family shelters the City pays for in full, a third to half full", "seconds": 142.6, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "db8073aec8fed756", "words": 371, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "San Francisco pays Hamilton Families to run a 44-bed emergency centre for homeless families.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.73, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "260 Golden Gate Avenue", "a": ["Hamilton Families emergency centre", "44 beds"], "b": ["in use, 12 September 2025", "?"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["44-bed"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.8, 1.12, 1.53, 2.05, 2.19, 2.4, 2.5, 3.26, 3.85, 4.19, 4.38, 4.79]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "On 12 September 2025, how many of those beds did the department count in use?", "t0": 5.85, "t1": 12.31, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "260 Golden Gate Avenue", "a": ["Hamilton Families emergency centre", "44 beds"], "b": ["in use, 12 September 2025", "?"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.53, 1.12, 1.5, 2.7, 2.83, 2.95, 3.03, 3.29, 3.7, 3.82, 3.91, 4.4, 4.84, 5.17]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "Five.", "t0": 12.31, "t1": 13.18, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "5 of 44", "label": "beds occupied, 12 September 2025", "sub": "Hamilton Families Emergency Center"}, "emph": ["Five"], "wt": [0.04]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["status"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 13.7, "t1": 15.64, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.18, 0.3, 1.04, 1.18, 1.28]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every count here is from the homelessness department’s own occupancy reports.", "t0": 15.76, "t1": 19.23, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.56, 0.77, 0.88, 1.01, 1.09, 1.56, 2.11, 2.32, 2.92]}, {"scene": "how", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "actors"], "text": "The department pays nonprofits to run family shelters, and it places the families itself.", "t0": 19.45, "t1": 24.27, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "How a family shelter is paid", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Department of Homelessness and Supportive Housing", "sub": "funds the shelters; places families"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Hamilton Families", "sub": "260 Golden Gate Avenue"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Mission Action, Inc.", "sub": "Downtown High School"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.47, 0.8, 1.39, 1.51, 1.67, 2.07, 3.09, 3.19, 3.33, 3.71, 3.85, 4.28]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "Six counts, from September 2025 to June 2026.", "t0": 24.49, "t1": 29.13, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Hamilton emergency centre: beds occupied, of 44", "rows": [["12 Sep 2025", "5"], ["26 Nov 2025", "6"], ["16 Dec 2025", "8"], ["16 Mar 2026", "23"], ["13 Apr 2026", "32"], ["15 Jun 2026", "21"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 1.09, 1.24, 1.64, 1.91, 2.82, 3.2, 3.5, 3.76]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Through December: 5, 6 and 8 beds in use.", "t0": 29.25, "t1": 32.77, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Hamilton emergency centre: beds occupied, of 44", "rows": [["12 Sep 2025", "5"], ["26 Nov 2025", "6"], ["16 Dec 2025", "8"], ["16 Mar 2026", "23"], ["13 Apr 2026", "32"], ["15 Jun 2026", "21"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 1.01, 2.05, 2.23, 2.38, 2.67, 2.96, 3.08]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Then 23, 32 and 21.", "t0": 32.77, "t1": 36.8, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Hamilton emergency centre: beds occupied, of 44", "rows": [["12 Sep 2025", "5"], ["26 Nov 2025", "6"], ["16 Dec 2025", "8"], ["16 Mar 2026", "23"], ["13 Apr 2026", "32"], ["15 Jun 2026", "21"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.72, 1.93, 2.76, 3.45]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Across all six, the centre was 36 percent full.", "t0": 36.92, "t1": 40.26, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "36%", "label": "of the centre’s beds in use over the six counts", "sub": "95 of 264 bed-counts"}, "emph": ["36 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.4, 0.68, 1.35, 1.45, 1.78, 1.97, 2.45, 2.88]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "The 27 family rooms under the same grant were 89 percent full.", "t0": 40.38, "t1": 45.05, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Same grant, same dates", "a": ["emergency centre", "36%"], "b": ["27 family rooms", "89%"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["89 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.72, 1.07, 1.37, 1.49, 1.61, 1.98, 2.53, 2.77, 3.2, 3.68]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The second site: a stay-over programme for school-district families, at Downtown High School.", "t0": 45.27, "t1": 50.33, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Downtown High School", "kicker": "Stay-over programme", "sub": "80 beds for families of school-district students"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.42, 1.08, 1.46, 1.87, 2.38, 2.52, 3.14, 3.77, 4.0, 4.44, 4.6]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[5]"], "text": "Mission Action runs it under a three-year grant of 8,360,615 dollars, for 80 beds.", "t0": 50.45, "t1": 55.67, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Downtown High School", "kicker": "Stay-over programme", "sub": "80 beds for families of school-district students"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.72, 0.98, 1.11, 1.37, 1.43, 1.87, 2.22, 2.31, 2.56, 2.72, 3.03, 3.17, 3.53, 4.35, 4.44, 4.75]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[1]"], "text": "In use: 53 in September, falling to 21 by June. That’s 26 percent.", "t0": 55.79, "t1": 62.55, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Downtown High School: beds occupied, of 80", "rows": [["12 Sep 2025", "53"], ["26 Nov 2025", "53"], ["16 Dec 2025", "28"], ["16 Mar 2026", "31"], ["13 Apr 2026", "23"], ["15 Jun 2026", "21"]]}, "emph": ["26 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.68, 1.77, 1.99, 2.98, 3.23, 3.33, 3.9, 4.16, 4.71, 5.52, 6.15]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "On the same dates, the department’s other family shelters were 87 percent full.", "t0": 62.67, "t1": 67.32, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Same six reports", "a": ["other family shelters", "87%"], "b": ["all other shelters", "94%"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["87 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.22, 0.44, 1.13, 1.21, 1.74, 1.96, 2.29, 2.79, 3.15, 3.83, 4.24]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "Every other shelter in the reports: 94 percent.", "t0": 67.44, "t1": 70.86, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Same six reports", "a": ["other family shelters", "87%"], "b": ["all other shelters", "94%"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.43, 0.75, 0.81, 0.92, 1.59, 2.73]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "Did the money follow the beds? What did the two grants get in fiscal 2026?", "t0": 71.08, "t1": 76.67, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Fiscal 2026", "kicker": "Did the money follow the beds?", "sub": "payments under the two grants"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.21, 0.43, 0.79, 0.92, 1.8, 2.21, 2.34, 2.47, 2.65, 3.17, 3.44, 3.62, 3.94, 4.21]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[6]"], "text": "5,336,042 dollars.", "t0": 76.67, "t1": 79.52, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$5,336,042", "label": "paid in fiscal 2026 under the two grants", "sub": "$3,919,375 Hamilton · $1,416,667 stay-over"}, "emph": ["5,336,042"], "wt": [0.04, 0.7, 0.98, 1.35, 1.6, 2.24]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "The Hamilton grant requires it to check in 95 percent of the beds reserved.", "t0": 80.04, "t1": 83.64, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "“shall check in at least 95 percent of all beds reserved”", "kicker": "Hamilton grant budget, 2023"}, "emph": ["95 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.4, 0.72, 1.1, 1.18, 1.32, 1.58, 1.72, 2.18, 2.5, 2.56, 2.67, 3.0]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Per bed in use, across both its programmes,", "t0": 83.76, "t1": 86.72, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "per occupied bed a night, fiscal 2026", "a": ["260 Golden Gate grant", "about $270"], "b": ["other shelters, renewal list", "$88 to $143"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.45, 0.7, 1.25, 1.72, 2.03, 2.25]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Hamilton’s grant came to about 270 dollars a night.", "t0": 86.72, "t1": 91.03, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "per occupied bed a night, fiscal 2026", "a": ["260 Golden Gate grant", "about $270"], "b": ["other shelters, renewal list", "$88 to $143"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["270 dollars"], "wt": [0.04, 0.8, 1.09, 1.38, 1.49, 1.96, 2.4, 2.76, 3.28, 3.76, 3.94]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why"], "text": "The department’s renewal list prices other shelters at 88 to 143.", "t0": 91.15, "t1": 96.21, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "per occupied bed a night, fiscal 2026", "a": ["260 Golden Gate grant", "about $270"], "b": ["other shelters, renewal list", "$88 to $143"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.57, 0.93, 1.26, 1.7, 1.92, 2.49, 2.69, 3.44, 3.7, 3.83, 4.12]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "timeline[9]"], "text": "On 1 July 2026, it re-signed Hamilton for two more years. For how much?", "t0": 96.33, "t1": 102.59, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "1 July 2026", "kicker": "Re-signed", "sub": "Hamilton Families, two more years"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.45, 0.76, 1.09, 2.36, 2.49, 2.97, 3.43, 3.61, 3.77, 4.06, 4.73, 5.23, 5.45]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "story[3]"], "text": "9,997,940 dollars, just under the line that needs a Board vote.", "t0": 102.59, "t1": 106.59, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$9,997,940", "label": "new two-year Hamilton agreement", "sub": "just under the line that needs a Board vote"}, "emph": ["just under"], "wt": [0.04, 0.54, 0.82, 1.11, 2.1, 2.3, 2.54, 2.66, 2.94, 3.03, 3.29, 3.37, 3.66]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[7]"], "text": "Three reports in a row print the centre’s rate as 23 percent.", "t0": 106.81, "t1": 110.34, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "o0", "kicker": "HSH occupancy report · 12 September 2025", "text": "Hamilton Families Emergency Center · 44 beds · 5 occupied · rate 23%", "mark": "23%"}, "emph": ["23 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.62, 0.7, 0.81, 1.12, 1.41, 1.5, 1.85, 2.17, 2.44, 2.93]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "Their own counts, 5, 6 and 8 of 44, make it 11 to 18 percent.", "t0": 110.46, "t1": 116.32, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "o0", "kicker": "HSH occupancy report · 12 September 2025", "text": "Hamilton Families Emergency Center · 44 beds · 5 occupied · rate 23%", "mark": "23%"}, "emph": ["11 to 18 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.32, 1.01, 1.67, 2.0, 2.31, 2.7, 2.96, 4.14, 4.27, 4.36, 4.67, 4.88, 5.19]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["next[3]"], "text": "The reports don't explain the gap.", "t0": 116.44, "t1": 118.2, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Why the reports print 23% for the emergency centre on three dates when the counts give 11% to 18%."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.52, 0.92, 1.17, 1.32]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["innocent[0]"], "text": "There are plain reasons. The department, not the grantee, places the families.", "t0": 118.42, "t1": 123.03, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "Plain reasons it could happen", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The department", "sub": "places the families"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Rooms, not beds", "sub": "a family of three in a four-bed room"}, {"art": "calendar", "name": "The school year", "sub": "fills and empties the stay-over"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.31, 0.6, 1.25, 1.65, 2.38, 2.55, 2.66, 3.59, 3.95, 4.07]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["innocent[1]"], "text": "A family of three in a room with four beds leaves a bed counted empty.", "t0": 123.15, "t1": 127.37, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "Plain reasons it could happen", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "The department", "sub": "places the families"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Rooms, not beds", "sub": "a family of three in a four-bed room"}, {"art": "calendar", "name": "The school year", "sub": "fills and empties the stay-over"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.43, 0.55, 1.05, 1.31, 1.38, 1.58, 1.79, 2.1, 2.53, 2.91, 3.01, 3.27, 3.74]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Nothing here says any provider billed for services it did not deliver.", "t0": 127.49, "t1": 131.24, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Why the two sites ran low", "Whether either grant was cut to match", "That any provider billed for services it did not deliver"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.53, 0.8, 1.0, 1.46, 1.8, 2.01, 2.64, 2.85, 3.01, 3.27]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? Daily counts at both sites, with referrals, and the grantees’ invoices.", "t0": 131.36, "t1": 136.78, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Daily occupancy at both sites, with referrals made and refused"}, {"who": "", "what": "Both grantees’ invoices and budget revisions for fiscal 2026"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.24, 0.54, 1.22, 1.65, 1.98, 2.13, 2.41, 2.94, 3.13, 3.84, 3.96, 4.05, 4.74]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No regulator has ruled on these shelters.", "t0": 136.9, "t1": 139.02, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.63, 0.84, 1.16, 1.28, 1.5]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 139.14, "t1": 141.66, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.37, 0.44, 0.54, 1.23, 1.62, 1.78]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "44 beds", "how": "How the shelters are paid", "lead1": "Lead 1 · 260 Golden Gate", "lead2": "Lead 2 · Downtown High School", "lead3": "Lead 3 · paid, then re-signed", "lead4": "Lead 4 · the printed rate", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "terminal", "hook": "contrast"}